# OSINT & Investigative Workflow Study

## Objective

Develop a professional, ethical, and repeatable workflow for open-source research and investigative analysis using publicly available information.

The goal of this project is not to access private systems, bypass controls, or perform unauthorized activity. The goal is to practice structured research, source validation, documentation, and analytical reporting in a way that can support IT operations, legal operations, compliance, fraud review, security support, and investigative analyst work.

---

## Why This Project Matters

Many technical and operational problems are not solved by tools alone. They require asking the right questions, gathering accurate information, validating sources, identifying patterns, and explaining findings clearly.

This project demonstrates the ability to:

- Work through incomplete information
- Separate assumptions from verified facts
- Organize findings into a clear structure
- Build timelines from scattered data
- Evaluate credibility of sources
- Document conclusions in a professional format

